// needed. A second, blank/unused glyph entry for 'D' is included solely to
// make first != last: TFT_eSPI's setFreeFont() (TFT_eSPI.cpp) computes the
// font's ascent/descent (glyph_ab/glyph_bb, used to convert a TL_DATUM y
// coordinate into the glyph's actual baseline) via
// `numChars = last - first; for (c = 0; c < numChars; c++) ...` - with
// first == last (a genuinely single-glyph font) numChars is 0, that loop
